PCCS optimized async upsert V2 E2E gas and runtime-size record
Recorded: 2026-05-26

Scope note:
- Targeted SGX/TDX double-upsert E2E and on-chain PCCS runtime sizes were refreshed after the latest gas optimization.
- Full FMSPC regression was rerun on 2026-05-26 with TCB_EVALS=19,20,21; 151 of 153 rows passed and the two failures are Intel PCS 404 responses for eval=19 FMSPC 20A06E050000.

Sources:
- SGX double-upsert E2E: logs/sgx-e2e.log
- TDX double-upsert E2E: logs/tdx-e2e.log
- Full FMSPC regression: logs/all-available-fmspc.log
- Full FMSPC gas summary: logs/all-available-fmspc-summary.log
- Runtime sizes: forge build --sizes in automata-on-chain-pccs and automata-dcap-attestation/evm

Notes:
- Dedicated SGX/TDX E2E sections list every charged transaction individually; Full FMSPC regression also records per-row total gas derived from those tx gas values.
- Quote verification is executed through eth_call in these E2E runs, so it has no charged transaction gas.
- EIP-170 runtime code size limit: 24,576 bytes.

